	Changelog

Newest first. Nothing here has been released yet; tagging v0.1.0 is what fires
.github/workflows/release.yml.


0.1.0
-----

The first version that boots a bare metal guest, passes its own test suite and
builds an installable APK in CI.

The emulator. RV64IMAFDC in C11 with no dependencies beyond libc and libm.
src/cpu has the core, the CSR file, the trap path and the FP unit. src/mmu does
Sv39, Sv48 and Sv57 with superpages and a direct mapped TLB. src/bus is a flat
sorted region table. src/devices has an ns16550a UART, a CLINT driven by the
host clock, a PLIC, the virtio-mmio transport with a split virtqueue, and
virtio-blk. src/loader reads ELF64 and raw blobs and builds the FDT in C.
src/vm assembles the machine, runs the loop and implements the SBI calls.

Tests. 31 suites and 585 assertions against a harness that builds a real bus,
MMU, CPU, CLINT, PLIC and UART and emits guest instructions into it.

Android. One Activity, three custom Views, no third party dependencies at all.
The VM runs on its own thread; input reaches it through a lock free ring and
vm.running is atomic. The release APK is 65 KB.

Build. A plain GNU Makefile with MODE=release|debug|sanity, WERROR=1 and
TEST_ARGS. scripts/build.sh, scripts/test.sh and scripts/clean.sh wrap it.
tools/mkrootfs.sh, tools/fetch_kernel.sh and tools/run.sh build and boot a
Debian guest. Five GitHub Actions workflows: build, test, lint, android and
release.

Tracing. RVM_TRACE_FROM and --trace-from open the instruction trace at one
guest PC and drop everything before it.

Fixes worth recording, because each one is easy to walk into again.

CSR_TIME read as zero. clint_tick() advances mtime and returns the MSIP and
MTIP bits it drives. vm_run() and the test harness both assigned that return
value to cpu.hw_time, which csr.c serves for CSR_TIME, so rdtime returned
interrupt bits instead of mtime. The Linux riscv clocksource is rdtime. The
harness had a second copy of the same mistake and also dropped MSIP.

The run loop did 385 ns per instruction. Two things ran on every retired
instruction and neither needed to. pump_input() is a read() syscall on stdin
and the clint refresh is a clock_gettime(). Both are now done every 256
instructions and immediately whenever a device moves an interrupt line. Separately,
best_source() scanned all 64 PLIC sources twice per refresh to answer what is
almost always no source. Together: 2.60 MIPS to 32.39 MIPS on a 20 million
instruction nop loop.

--stats reported throughput 1000 times too low. It computed instructions per
nanosecond and called the result MIPS.

Signed overflow in addw, subw, addiw and mul. RISC-V specifies a wrap, C
specifies undefined behaviour. These now compute in the matching unsigned type.
Found by the sanitizers job.

sext() and imm_clui() shifted negative signed values left. Found by UBSan.

The ELF builder's PUT16, PUT32 and PUT64 macros shifted the caller's
expression, so PUT64(40, 0) shifted a 32 bit int by 32. Found by UBSan.

make coverage had clean as a prerequisite, which under -j deletes build/ while
parallel compiles are writing into it. It now runs two sequential sub-makes.

scripts/*.sh only accepted -j 4, so CI's -j"$(nproc)" was rejected as an
unknown option.

dtb/rvm.dts referenced &plic on a node that carried only a hand written phandle
property, which dtc rejects.

android/settings.gradle.kts declared plugin repositories but no project
repositories, so AGP could not resolve its own aapt2.

android-actions/setup-android@v3 installs the retired tools package by default
and fails without an explicit package list.

The Android manifest declared an ACTION_VIEW filter for octet-stream that
nothing handled, and an octet-stream URI cannot say whether it is a kernel or a
disk image. Removed. Kernels and images enter through ACTION_OPEN_DOCUMENT,
where the user picks the file.

make lint is -fsyntax-only and so never saw two warnings that only appear once
gcc folds constants at -O2. scripts/test.sh grew --werror, which CI uses.
